VALUES (652, '0', $t$ASK 652: the press ledger counts and labels only the pressed verses, not the verses inside a press line$t$,
  $t$The premise reader in D4 Build, Panel Build and Build Independent Verdict looped over every reference in a premise's PRESSED WITH block, including the [L3] verse and the MEANS words of each press line. PRS.premise classes only the pressed verses, so every other reference fell into "UNPROVEN, not a witness (no MEANS sentence)" and was counted toward the cap of 8 pressed verses, which could cut real presses as "over the cap". In run 42528 the judges' ledger against the challenger said 25 verses of the Oracle's presses were "UNPROVEN, not a witness (ruling 398)"; all 25 are layer verses inside the Oracle's presses, 22 of whose 23 pressed verses are PROVEN, and in premise 3 the cap set aside the Oracle's proven press Job 14:1. To the Oracle, Matthew 1:20 and Galatians 4:4 were listed as costless when they are [L3] lines. Change, the same statement in each of the three copies: when PRS.premise has classed the premise, a reference that is neither one of its pressed verses nor one of its presses past the cap is passed over: not counted as a press, not counted to the cap, not labelled. Expected effect: the ledger given to the judges and the list given to the Oracle name only presses. The Shared Library reader already worked this way. Not changed: ruling 398, the cap, the WALL-2024 floor, a model setting, reasoning. (plan rev 1, ask652/w4/plan652.md md5 c82c1d69)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$One build, one card and one write carry ASK 651 and ASK 652 together: target 1aa15175, written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 09:09 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12127; audit 42304), engine 7f4e5503 to 50ade174 (426 nodes; the child aad0ad9c unchanged), build graded PASS by W1 (Wall 12108: W1 ran b651 and b652 on its own live copy and the result equals the target in every node parameter and in the connections; only D4 Build, Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict and Shared Library change) and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 12129). IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. For ASK 652: plan rev 0 (bce5be7f) was graded FAIL F1 by W1 (Wall 12101: PRS.premise has its own cap of 8 and puts presses past it in PRSP.over, so the planned filter would have skipped real over-cap presses and the "over the cap of 8 pressed verses" line would have stopped printing). Rev 1 accepts a key in PRSP.verses or PRSP.over and was graded PASS (Wall 12103); rev 0's file was overwritten by rev 1. In the build, test 28 proves the cap case (10 real presses give 8 counted and "over the cap" names the two past it). Judge ledger for 42528, before and after, read by W1 (Wall 12108): the Oracle's layer verses are no longer called "UNPROVEN ... no MEANS sentence"; Job 14:1 and Acts 13:33 are counted as presses; both WALL-2024 floor items stay. W4's counts (Wall 12105): 25 layer verses lose the label; verse counts per premise go from 7/7/8/8/8/8 to 3/3/5/4/4/4; the fix is side-neutral (in 42373 the challenger's presses Luke 1:32 and Hebrews 7:10 are counted instead of falling over the cap). One judge-facing line the plan did not name (W1's note for the card, Wall 12108): layer verses written in a premise head now appear as "other verses the premise names (informational, not witnesses)"; it does not change the count rule. Left out of this ASK by W4 as a ruling question: Luke 1:34 in premise 4 of 42528, a pressed verse that fails the WALL-2024 floor. NOT CHECKED by W1: W4's replay figures; the 18-of-18 match of the "before" replay to the live Panel Build output; the Library Check hashes; audit 42304. Open: two clean live runs. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). FIRST RUN, NO FAULT LINE SEEN; THE MARK ITSELF NOT READ. W4: no "not a witness ... no MEANS sentence" line stands in the enforcer prompts. The panel's first prompt, where the press ledger stands, is not in the tables W4 read and was not read, so the ledger's counts are not shown. NOT CHECKED by W1. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
  '12100, 12101, 12102, 12103, 12105, 12108, 12127, 12129, 12139, 12145, 12152, 12787, 12791, 12797, 12799, 12800, 12802, 12803, 12804, 12789',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), 240,
  to_jsonb($t$W4's write card (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58F12ck7RxDR9wiG7wni57j5, "Write ASK 651 + 652 to the live engine?"): he pressed "Write it" at 09:09 CST 2026-11-25 (one card and one write for ASK 651 and ASK 652). Card text, press and time are from W4's facts file; W3 did not read the card or the press. There was no build card: the build was offline files only, and the card came after the build grade.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "source": "W4's facts file aar/w3/cards_641_to_652_from_w4.md; W3 did not read the card or the press. One card and one write cover ASK 651 and ASK 652.", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58F12ck7RxDR9wiG7wni57j5", "options": {"Hold": "Next run keeps the false UNPROVEN labels and the false costless list (25 such labels were in the 42528 judge text).", "Write it": "Stops the engine telling judges proven verses are \"not a witness\" and telling the Oracle proven presses cost nothing. Reverts with one file."}, "question": "Write ASK 651 + 652 to the live engine?", "press_time": "09:09 CST 2026-11-25", "message_above_the_card": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58YEDWGeV3txREtJW5gMFKEk"}$j$::jsonb,
